My mother looks at me on the phone.
She has never heard my side of the story before.
"What did you do at the airport back then?" she asks.
I take a deep breath and tell her the truth.
After the goodbye, I looked at you through the glass.
I watched you for a very long time.
Then I waited alone in the queue.
Back then I was very afraid of the long flight.
So I counted the people in the queue.
That calmed me down a little.
After that I checked my backpack.
Then at the gate I cried quietly.
I have never told anyone that before.
Mama looks at me affectionately through the screen.
She has listened to me completely silently.
Now she wants to tell her side of the story.
